Sea Training for All India Naval Cadets at Mumbai! ⚓🇮🇳

122 NCC Naval Cadets, including 61 Girl Cadets, from across India completed an immersive 12-day Sea Training Camp under #NCCMaharashtra, with steadfast support from @indiannavy & HQ #WNC.

From frontline warships, submarines and naval aviation to life at sea, the camp offered invaluable exposure to the Navy’s ethos and operational excellence.

Coming on the heels of Sea Attachment, and ahead of scuba diving training, this reflects WNC’s exceptional commitment to partnering with NCC in empowering future-ready youth.

Addressing the cadets onboard Indian Navy ship, Maj Gen Vivek Tyagi, ADG highlighted value of the tremendous exposure to the passionate future leaders and the ethos of #NationFirst.
